HHIISSTTOORRYY
       Before  Netpbm  10.15  (April 2003), ppnnmmccoolloorrmmaapp used a lot more memory
       for large images because it kept the  entire  input  image  in  memory.
       Now,  it  processes  it  a row at a time, but because it sometimes must
       make multiple passes through the image, it first copies the input  into
       a temporary seekable file if it is not already in a seekable file.

       ppnnmmccoolloorrmmaapp first appeared in Netpbm 9.23 (January 2002).  Before that,
       its function was available only as part of  the  function  of  ppnnmmqquuaanntt
       (which  was  derived from the much older ppppmmqquuaanntt).  Color quantization
       really has two main subfunctions, so Netpbm 9.23 split it out into  two
       separate  programs:  ppnnmmccoolloorrmmaapp  and ppnnmmrreemmaapp and then Netpbm 9.24 re‐
       placed ppnnmmqquuaanntt with a program that simply calls ppnnmmccoolloorrmmaapp  and  ppnnmm‐‐
       rreemmaapp.


